# Cairn commits from Cursor Agent

Cairn's `prepare-commit-msg` hook calls `claude` / `cursor-agent` for distillation.
The default Cursor Agent sandbox injects `HTTP(S)_PROXY` to a local seatbelt proxy;
`cursor-agent` then fails with `SSL EPROTO … packet length too long`, and the
record collapses to metadata-only.

When running `git commit` (or any command that triggers cairn hooks) from the
Agent shell:

- Request `required_permissions: ["full_network"]` at minimum
- Prefer `["all"]` if the commit also needs unrestricted git hook filesystem access
- Do not commit under the default sandbox — distillation will not reach the API

A normal external terminal is fine; only the Agent sandbox breaks this.
